# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Web UI dependencies are rebuilt from the committed package lock.
/webui/node_modules/
/webui/*.tsbuildinfo

# Private project materials: official register maps, generated catalog data,
# internal specifications, and agent instructions remain local only.
#
# /docs/ itself is deliberately NOT ignored as a whole directory — git
# cannot "un-ignore" individual files inside an ignored directory (a
# documented limitation: it never descends into one to check exceptions),
# so every actually-private document under docs/ is named directly
# instead. docs/point-reference.md and docs/open-questions.md are
# generated straight from catalog/point_catalog.json (Task 8 review:
# both expose the full derived register map — every point, IEC-104/
# Modbus address, type, range, and setpoint — which is exactly the kind
# of internal data this section already keeps local-only elsewhere) and
# stay private artifacts: `make generate` still writes them locally (see
# codegen/gen_docs.py, catalog/validate_catalog.py), they are simply
# never committed. Only docs/README.md (a plain operator guide, no
# catalog data of its own) is tracked.
/m261-registermap/
/catalog/point_catalog.json
/catalog/validation_report.md
/docs/AGENT-TASK.md
/docs/AGENT-CODE-REVIEW.md
/docs/point-reference.md
/docs/open-questions.md

# Credentials and local runtime configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
secrets/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Go
/simulator/**/*.exe
/simulator/bin/

# OS
.DS_Store

# NOTE: generated code in gen/ is intentionally tracked, not ignored.
.venv/
